-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- LAYER 1, part ssc2, module 5 of 6: ss 37, 38, 39, 39A and 39C (widowed mother's allowance, widow's pension,
-- widowed parent's allowance, and their rates). ss 36, 36A and 39B are blank in this text.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-1992-4.txt, a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- Money is a NUMBER in pounds; a rate is weekly unless the name says otherwise.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the Act answering in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered".
-- A woman's "age" at a time is her age in completed years; "over the age of 45" is "has attained" 45
-- (s 173(a)), which is a completed-years age of 45 or more; "under the age of 65" is 64 or less.

§ `Part II -- Bereavement benefits (ss 37, 38, 39, 39A, 39C)`

§§ `s 37 Widowed mother's allowance: deaths before 9 April 2001`

-- Kleene negation, "and" and "or" over MAYBE BOOLEAN: a limb the text answers "no" decides the whole even
-- when another limb is unknown; otherwise an unknown limb leaves the whole unknown.
-- src:1073 | (1) A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance at the rate determined in accordance with section 39 below if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed mother’s allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and either—
-- src:1074 | (a) the woman is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (2) below; or
-- src:1075 | (b) the woman is pregnant by her late husband; or
-- src:1076 | (c) if the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before the time of his death, the woman is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person other than her husband, or as the result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs.
@ref s 37(1) (src:1073-1076)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37 both` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 37(1) (src:1073-1076)
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37 either` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER b
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (A1) This section applies only in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001.
-- src:1072 | (A1) This section applies only in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001.
@ref s 37(A1) (src:1072)
GIVEN `the day on which the woman's husband died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the woman's husband died` BELOW (Date 9 4 2001)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001."

-- (1)(c) if the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before the time of his death,
-- the woman is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of
-- some person other than her husband, or as the result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo,
-- of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs. (Also used by s 39A(2)(b)(ii), which reads
-- "her late husband" as including the deceased cohabiting partner.)
-- src:1076 | (c) if the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before the time of his death, the woman is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person other than her husband, or as the result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs.
@ref s 37(1)(c) (src:1076)
GIVEN `the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before the time of his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the woman is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person other than her husband, or as the result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described` MEANS
    IF `the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before the time of his death` AND `the woman is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person other than her husband, or as the result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance ... if ... and either— ... (c) if the woman and her late husband were residing together ..."

-- (2) A child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection if the child or qualifying young person
-- is either (a) a son or daughter of the woman and her late husband; or (b) a child or qualifying young person
-- in respect of whom her late husband was immediately before his death entitled to child benefit; or (c) if the
-- woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before his death, a child or qualifying young
-- person in respect of whom she was then entitled to child benefit. (The text shows an ellipsis after "if".)
-- src:1077 | (2) A child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection if ... the child or qualifying young person is either—
-- src:1078 | (a) a son or daughter of the woman and her late husband; or
-- src:1079 | (b) a child or qualifying young person in respect of whom her late husband was immediately before his death entitled to child benefit; or
-- src:1080 | (c) if the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before his death, a child or qualifying young person in respect of whom she was then entitled to child benefit.
@ref s 37(2) (src:1077-1080)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is a son or daughter of the woman and her late husband` IS A BOOLEAN
      `her late husband was immediately before his death entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before his death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she was then entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(2) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    IF `the child or qualifying young person is a son or daughter of the woman and her late husband`
       OR `her late husband was immediately before his death entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person`
       OR (`the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before his death` AND `she was then entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection if ... the child or qualifying young person is either—"

-- (1) A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance at the rate determined
-- under s 39 if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed mother's allowance
-- specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 (seam S1) and either (a) the woman is entitled to child
-- benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within (2); or (b) she is pregnant by her
-- late husband; or (c) the circumstances in (1)(c).
-- src:1073 | (1) A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance at the rate determined in accordance with section 39 below if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed mother’s allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and either—
-- src:1074 | (a) the woman is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (2) below; or
-- src:1075 | (b) the woman is pregnant by her late husband; or
-- src:1076 | (c) if the woman and her late husband were residing together immediately before the time of his death, the woman is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person other than her husband, or as the result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs.
@ref s 37(1) (src:1073-1076)
GIVEN `s 37(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the woman has been widowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a widowed mother's allowance are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the woman is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the woman is pregnant by her late husband` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(1) the woman is entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` MEANS
    `s 37 both` `s 37(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband`
        (`s 37 both` (JUST `the woman has been widowed`)
            (`s 37 both` `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a widowed mother's allowance are satisfied`
                (`s 37 either` (JUST `the woman is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (2)`)
                    (`s 37 either` (JUST `the woman is pregnant by her late husband`) `s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described`))))
    -- JUST FALSE when a condition fails: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance at the rate determined in accordance with section 39 below if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions ... and either—"

-- (3) The widow shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she remarries or forms a civil
-- partnership, but, subject to that, she shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which
-- she satisfies the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c). Taken a day at a time: a day after the day
-- she remarries or forms a civil partnership is outside; before then she is entitled on a day on which she
-- satisfies the requirements.
-- src:1081 | (3) The widow shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she remarries or forms a civil partnership, but, subject to that, she shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she satisfies the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) above.
@ref s 37(3) (src:1081)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which she remarries or forms a civil partnership` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `she satisfies the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(3) the widow is entitled to the allowance on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which she remarries or forms a civil partnership`
    WHEN JUST remarried THEN
        IF `the day` ABOVE remarried
        THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The widow shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she remarries or forms a civil partnership"
        ELSE CONSIDER `she satisfies the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) on the day`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "she shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she satisfies the requirements"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `she satisfies the requirements of subsection (1)(a), (b) or (c) on the day`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "she shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she satisfies the requirements"

-- (4) A widowed mother's allowance shall not be payable (a) for any period before the day on which the
-- widow's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the
-- Administration Act (not among the sources); or (b) for any period during which she and a person she is not
-- married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil
-- partners.
-- src:1082 | (4) A widowed mother’s allowance shall not be payable—
-- src:1083 | (a) for any period falling before the day on which the widow’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act; ... or
-- src:1084 | (b) for any period during which she and a person whom she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref s 37(4) (src:1082-1084)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the widow's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `she and a person whom she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 37(4) the allowance is payable for the day` MEANS
    IF `she and a person whom she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners on the day`
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A widowed mother’s allowance shall not be payable— ... (b) for any period during which she and a person whom she is not married to ... are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners."
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which the widow's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act`
         WHEN JUST commencing THEN
             IF `the day` BELOW commencing
             THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A widowed mother’s allowance shall not be payable— (a) for any period falling before the day on which the widow’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing"
             ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when the allowance is not payable
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the commencing day is for section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act

§§ `s 38 Widow's pension: deaths before 9 April 2001`

-- (A1) This section applies only in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001.
-- src:1086 | (A1) This section applies only in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001.
@ref s 38(A1) (src:1086)
GIVEN `the day on which the woman's husband died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the woman's husband died` BELOW (Date 9 4 2001)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001."

-- (4) In the case of a widow whose late husband died before 11th April 1988 and who either (a) was over 40
-- but under 55 at the time of her husband's death or (b) is over 40 but under 55 at the time when she ceases
-- to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance, subsection (1) has effect as if for "45" there were
-- substituted "40". The same case is the one s 39(6) reads "55" as "50" for.
-- src:1095 | (4) In the case of a widow whose late husband died before 11th April 1988 and who either—
-- src:1096 | (a) was over the age of 40 but under the age of 55 at the time of her husband’s death; or
-- src:1097 | (b) is over the age of 40 but under the age of 55 at the time when she ceases to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance,
-- src:1098 | subsection (1) above shall have effect as if for “45" there were substituted “40”.
@ref s 38(4) (src:1095-1098)
GIVEN `the day on which the woman's husband died` IS A DATE
      `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when her husband died` IS A NUMBER
      `the woman has ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF (`the day on which the woman's husband died` BELOW (Date 11 4 1988))
       AND ((`s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when her husband died` AT LEAST 40 AND `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when her husband died` BELOW 55)
            OR (`the woman has ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` AND `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` AT LEAST 40 AND `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` BELOW 55))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a widow whose late husband died before 11th April 1988 and who either— (a) ... or (b) ..."

@ref s 38(4) (src:1098)
GIVEN `s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 38(4) the lower age read in subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN 40
    OTHERWISE 45     -- subsection (1) as written: "over the age of 45"

-- (1) A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widow's pension at the rate determined under s 39 if
-- her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widow's pension specified in Schedule 3,
-- Part I, paragraph 5 (seam S1) and either (a) she was, at the husband's death, over the lower age (45, or 40
-- under (4)) but under 65; or (b) she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance at a time when she
-- was over that age but under 65.
-- src:1087 | (1) A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widow’s pension at the rate determined in accordance with section 39 below if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widow’s pension specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and either—
-- src:1088 | (a) she was, at the husband’s death, over the age of 45 but under the age of 65; or
-- src:1089 | (b) she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance at a time when she was over the age of 45 but under the age of 65.
@ref s 38(1) (src:1087-1089)
GIVEN `s 38(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the woman has been widowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a widow's pension are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 38(4) the lower age read in subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when her husband died` IS A NUMBER
      `the woman has ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(1) the woman is entitled to a widow's pension` MEANS
    `s 37 both` `s 38(A1) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband`
        (`s 37 both` (JUST `the woman has been widowed`)
            (`s 37 both` `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a widow's pension are satisfied`
                (JUST ((`s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when her husband died` AT LEAST `s 38(4) the lower age read in subsection (1)` AND `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when her husband died` BELOW 65)
                       OR (`the woman has ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` AND `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` AT LEAST `s 38(4) the lower age read in subsection (1)` AND `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` BELOW 65)))))
    -- JUST FALSE when a condition fails: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widow’s pension at the rate determined in accordance with section 39 below if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions ... and either—"

-- (2) The widow shall not be entitled to the pension for any period after she remarries or forms a civil
-- partnership, but, subject to that, she shall continue to be entitled to it until she attains pensionable
-- age. Taken a day at a time: after the day she remarries, or on or after the day she attains pensionable age,
-- the day is outside; otherwise she is entitled on a day if she was entitled under (1).
-- src:1090 | (2) The widow shall not be entitled to the pension for any period after she remarries or forms a civil partnership, but, subject to that, she shall continue to be entitled to it until she attains pensionable age.
@ref s 38(2) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the woman` IS A Person
      `the day on which she remarries or forms a civil partnership` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `s 38(1) the woman is entitled to a widow's pension` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(2) the widow is entitled to the pension on the day` MEANS
    IF (CONSIDER `the day on which she remarries or forms a civil partnership`
        WHEN JUST remarried THEN `the day` ABOVE remarried
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The widow shall not be entitled to the pension for any period after she remarries or forms a civil partnership"
    ELSE IF `the day` AT LEAST (`the woman`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)
         THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "she shall continue to be entitled to it until she attains pensionable age"
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 38(1) the woman is entitled to a widow's pension`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection continues an entitlement under (1); it does not itself grant one

-- (3) A widow's pension shall not be payable (a) for any period before the day on which the widow's
-- entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the
-- Administration Act; (b) for any period for which she is entitled to a widowed mother's allowance; or (c)
-- for any period during which she and a person she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are
-- living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
-- src:1091 | (3) A widow’s pension shall not be payable—
-- src:1092 | (a) for any period falling before the day on which the widow’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act;
-- src:1093 | (b) for any period for which she is entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance; ... or
-- src:1094 | (c) for any period during which she and a person whom she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref s 38(3) (src:1091-1094)
