      `the day on which the widow's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `she is entitled to a widowed mother's allowance for the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she and a person whom she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(3) the pension is payable for the day` MEANS
    IF `she is entitled to a widowed mother's allowance for the day`
       OR `she and a person whom she is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners on the day`
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A widow’s pension shall not be payable— ... (b) for any period for which she is entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance; ... or (c) for any period during which she and a person whom she is not married to ... are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners."
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which the widow's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing for that purpose by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act`
         WHEN JUST commencing THEN
             IF `the day` BELOW commencing
             THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A widow’s pension shall not be payable— (a) for any period falling before the day on which the widow’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing"
             ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when the pension is not payable
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the commencing day is for section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act

-- Seam S17 (asked by ssc3 s 48B): is the surviving spouse entitled, or treated by regulations as entitled, to a
-- widow's pension by virtue of this section, and at what weekly rate (the rate under s 39).
-- src:1087 | (1) A woman who has been widowed shall be entitled to a widow’s pension at the rate determined in accordance with section 39 below if her late husband satisfied the contribution conditions for a widow’s pension specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and either—
-- src:1088 | (a) she was, at the husband’s death, over the age of 45 but under the age of 65; or
-- src:1089 | (b) she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance at a time when she was over the age of 45 but under the age of 65.
