§§ `s 39 Rate of widowed mother's allowance and widow's pension`

-- (1) The weekly rate of (a) a widowed mother's allowance, (b) a widow's pension, is determined in accordance
-- with ss 44 to 45B as they apply in the case of a Category A retirement pension, subject to s 39 and s 46.
-- Seam S15: ssc3 s 46(2) asks whether the additional pension falls to be calculated under s 45 "by virtue of
-- section 39(1)". It does for these two benefits.
-- src:1100 | (1) The weekly rate of—
-- src:1101 | (a) a widowed mother’s allowance,
-- src:1102 | (b) a widow’s pension,
-- src:1103 | shall be determined in accordance with the provisions of sections 44 to 45B ... below as they apply in the case of a Category A retirement pension, but subject, in particular, to the following provisions of this section and section 46 below.
@ref s 39(1) (src:1100-1103)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) the additional pension falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `widowed mother's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `widow's pension` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 39(1) speaks only of a widowed mother's allowance and a widow's pension

-- (2) In the application of ss 44 to 45B by virtue of (1): (a) where the woman's husband was over pensionable
-- age when he died, references to the pensioner are references to the husband; (b) where he was under
-- pensionable age when he died, references to the pensioner and the tax year in which he attained pensionable
-- age are references to the husband and the tax year in which he died.
-- src:1104 | (2) In the application of sections 44 to 45B ... below by virtue of subsection (1) above—
-- src:1105 | (a) where the woman’s husband was over pensionable age when he died, references in those sections to the pensioner shall be taken as references to the husband, and
-- src:1106 | (b) where the husband was under pensionable age when he died, references in those sections to the pensioner and the tax year in which he attained pensionable age shall be taken as references to the husband and the tax year in which he died.
@ref s 39(2) (src:1104-1106)
GIVEN `the husband` IS A Person
      `the day on which the husband died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39(2) the husband was over pensionable age when he died` MEANS
    `the day on which the husband died` AT LEAST (`the husband`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)

@ref s 39(2) (src:1105-1106)
GIVEN `the husband` IS A Person
      `the day on which the husband died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 39(2) the tax year read as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` MEANS
    IF `s 39(2) the husband was over pensionable age when he died` `the husband` `the day on which the husband died`
    THEN `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `s 23A(8) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the date begins` (`the husband`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)
    ELSE `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `s 23A(8) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the date begins` `the day on which the husband died`

-- (2A) In its application by virtue of (1), s 44(4) is read as if for the first amount specified in that
-- provision there were substituted a reference to the amount prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.
-- src:1107 | (2A) In its application by virtue of subsection (1) above, section 44(4) below is to be read as if for the first amount specified in that provision there were substituted a reference to the amount prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 39(2A) (src:1107)
GIVEN `the amount prescribed for the purposes of subsection (2A) in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 39(2A) the amount read in place of the first amount specified in section 44(4) in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount prescribed for the purposes of subsection (2A) in pounds`     -- NOTHING when not supplied: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the amount prescribed"

-- (5) For the purposes of (4) the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled is the time when
-- the woman's late husband died or, as the case may be, the time when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed
-- mother's allowance. A woman who qualifies under s 38(1)(a) qualified at her husband's death (fork F16).
-- src:1110 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4) above, the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled is the time when the woman’s late husband died or, as the case may be, the time when she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance.
@ref s 39(5) (src:1110)
GIVEN `she qualified for the widow's pension under section 38(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the husband died` IS A DATE
      `the day on which she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 39(5) the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled` MEANS
    IF `she qualified for the widow's pension under section 38(1)(a)`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the husband died`
    ELSE `the day on which she ceased to be entitled to a widowed mother's allowance`     -- NOTHING when she did not cease: NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the husband's death or the end of her widowed mother's allowance

-- (6) In the case of a widow whose late husband died before 11th April 1988 and who either (a) was over 40 but
-- under 55 at the time of her husband's death or (b) is over 40 but under 55 at the time when she ceases to be
-- entitled to a widowed mother's allowance, (4) has effect as if for "55" there were substituted "50", in
-- both places. It is the same case as s 38(4).
-- src:1111 | (6) In the case of a widow whose late husband died before 11th April 1988 and who either—
-- src:1112 | (a) was over the age of 40 but under the age of 55 at the time of her husband’s death; or
-- src:1113 | (b) is over the age of 40 but under the age of 55 at the time when she ceases to be entitled to a widowed mother’s allowance,
-- src:1114 | subsection (4) above shall have effect as if for “55" there were substituted “ 50 ”, in both places where it occurs.
@ref s 39(6) (src:1111-1114)
GIVEN `s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 38(4) the widow's case is one mentioned in subsection (4)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN 50
    OTHERWISE 55     -- subsection (4) as written: "under the age of 55"

-- (4) Where a widow's pension is payable to a woman who was under 55 (or 50 under (6)) at the time when the
-- applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled, the weekly rate is reduced by 7 per cent. of what it would
-- be apart from this subsection multiplied by the number of years by which her age at that time was less than
-- 55 (any fraction of a year being counted as a year). A woman whose completed years of age at that time are
-- A and who is under 55 is short by 55 less A years, counting any part of a year as a year.
-- src:1109 | (4) Where a widow’s pension is payable to a woman who was under the age of 55 at the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled, the weekly rate of the pension shall be reduced by 7 per cent. of what it would be apart from this subsection multiplied by the number of years by which her age at that time was less than 55 (any fraction of a year being counted as a year).
@ref s 39(4) (src:1109)
GIVEN `the weekly rate of the widow's pension apart from subsection (4) in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` IS A NUMBER
      `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years at the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 39(4) the weekly rate of the widow's pension after any reduction in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the weekly rate of the widow's pension apart from subsection (4) in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rate apart from this subsection is worked out under sections 44 to 45B
    WHEN JUST rate THEN
        IF `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years at the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled` BELOW `s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)`
        THEN JUST (rate MINUS (7% TIMES rate TIMES (`s 39(6) the age read in subsection (4)` MINUS `s 173(a) the woman's age in completed years at the time when the applicable qualifying condition was fulfilled`)))
        ELSE JUST rate     -- subsection (4) does not apply to a woman of 55 or over (50 or over under (6)): the rate stands

§§ `s 39A Widowed parent's allowance`

-- The kinds of survivor s 39A speaks of.
-- src:1121 | (2) The surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner shall be entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance at the rate determined in accordance with section 39C below if the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed parent’s allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and—
@ref s 39A(2) (src:1121)
DECLARE `s 39A Kind of survivor` IS ONE OF
    `s 39A the surviving spouse`
    `s 39A the surviving civil partner`
    `s 39A the surviving cohabiting partner`

-- (1) This section applies where (a) a person's spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner has died before
-- the day on which s 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force, (b) the person has not married or formed a
-- civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership after the death but before that day, and (c) the person is
-- under pensionable age on that day. That day is not in the sources: an input.
-- src:1116 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:1117 | (a) a person's spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner has died before the day on which section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force (but see subsection (1A)),
-- src:1118 | (b) the person has not married or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership after the death but before that day, and
-- src:1119 | (c) the person is under pensionable age on that day.
@ref s 39A(1) (src:1116-1119)
GIVEN `the day on which the person's spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the person has married or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership after the death but before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(1) the section applies` MEANS
    IF (`the day on which the person's spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` BELOW `the day on which section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force`)
       AND (NOT `the person has married or formed a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership after the death but before that day`)
       AND (`the day on which section 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 comes into force` BELOW (`the person`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where—"

-- (1A) This section does not apply in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001.
-- src:1120 | (1A) This section does not apply in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001.
@ref s 39A(1A) (src:1120)
GIVEN `the day on which the woman's husband died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(1A) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the woman's husband died` BELOW (Date 9 4 2001)
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001."
    ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says nothing about a death on or after 9 April 2001

-- (3) A child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection if the child or qualifying young person
-- is either (a) a son or daughter of the survivor and the deceased; or (b) a child or qualifying young person
-- in respect of whom the deceased was immediately before death entitled to child benefit; or (c) if the survivor
-- and the deceased were residing together immediately before death, a child or qualifying young person in
-- respect of whom the survivor was then entitled to child benefit.
-- src:1129 | (3) A child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection if ... the child or qualifying young person is either—
-- src:1130 | (a) a son or daughter of the surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner and the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner; or
-- src:1131 | (b) a child or qualifying young person in respect of whom the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner was immediately before his or her death entitled to child benefit; or
-- src:1132 | (c) if the surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner and the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner were residing together immediately before his or her death, a child or qualifying young person in respect of whom the surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner was then entitled to child benefit.
@ref s 39A(3) (src:1129-1132)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is a son or daughter of the survivor and the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased was immediately before death entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor and the deceased were residing together immediately before death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor was then entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(3) the child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection` MEANS
    IF `the child or qualifying young person is a son or daughter of the survivor and the deceased`
       OR `the deceased was immediately before death entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person`
       OR (`the survivor and the deceased were residing together immediately before death` AND `the survivor was then entitled to child benefit in respect of the child or qualifying young person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A child or qualifying young person falls within this subsection if ... the child or qualifying young person is either—"

-- (2)(a), (b), (c): the requirements. (a) the survivor is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or
-- qualifying young person within (3). (b) the surviving spouse or cohabiting partner is a woman who either
-- (i) is pregnant by her late husband or the deceased cohabiting partner, or (ii) if she and he were residing
-- together immediately before his death, is pregnant in circumstances falling within s 37(1)(c). (c) the
-- surviving civil partner or cohabiting partner is a woman who (i) was residing together with the deceased
-- immediately before the death and (ii) is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before
-- that time with the semen of some person, or of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, an egg in the
-- process of fertilisation, or sperm and eggs.
-- src:1121 | (2) The surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner shall be entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance at the rate determined in accordance with section 39C below if the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed parent’s allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and—
-- src:1122 | (a) the surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (3) below; ...
-- src:1123 | (b) the surviving spouse or cohabiting partner is a woman who either—
-- src:1124 | (i) is pregnant by her late husband or the deceased cohabiting partner, or
-- src:1125 | (ii) if she and he were residing together immediately before the time of his death, is pregnant in circumstances falling within section 37(1)(c) above (which is to be read as if the references to her late husband included a reference to the deceased cohabiting partner) or
-- src:1126 | (c) the surviving civil partner or cohabiting partner is a woman who—
-- src:1127 | (i) was residing together with the deceased civil partner or cohabiting partner immediately before the time of the death, and
-- src:1128 | (ii) is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person, or as a result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs.
@ref s 39A(2) (src:1121-1128)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 39A Kind of survivor`
      `the survivor is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is pregnant by the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the survivor was residing together with the deceased immediately before the time of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the survivor is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person, or as a result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(2) the survivor satisfies the requirements of paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` MEANS
    `s 37 either`
        (JUST `the survivor is entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person falling within subsection (3)`)
        (`s 37 either`
            (IF (kind EQUALS `s 39A the surviving spouse` OR kind EQUALS `s 39A the surviving cohabiting partner`) AND `the survivor is a woman`
             THEN `s 37 either` (JUST `the survivor is pregnant by the deceased`) `s 37(1)(c) the woman is pregnant in the circumstances described`
             ELSE JUST FALSE)     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the surviving spouse or cohabiting partner is a woman who either—"
            (IF (kind EQUALS `s 39A the surviving civil partner` OR kind EQUALS `s 39A the surviving cohabiting partner`) AND `the survivor is a woman`
             THEN JUST (`the survivor was residing together with the deceased immediately before the time of the death` AND `the survivor is pregnant as the result of being artificially inseminated before that time with the semen of some person, or as a result of the placing in her before that time of an embryo, of an egg in the process of fertilisation, or of sperm and eggs`)
             ELSE JUST FALSE))    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the surviving civil partner or cohabiting partner is a woman who—"

-- (2) The surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner shall be entitled to a widowed parent's
-- allowance at the rate determined under s 39C if the deceased satisfied the contribution conditions for a
-- widowed parent's allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 (seam S1) and (a), (b) or (c).
-- src:1121 | (2) The surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner shall be entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance at the rate determined in accordance with section 39C below if the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner satisfied the contribution conditions for a widowed parent’s allowance specified in Schedule 3, Part I, paragraph 5 and—
@ref s 39A(2) (src:1121)
GIVEN `s 39A(1) the section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 39A(1A) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a widowed parent's allowance are satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 39A(2) the survivor satisfies the requirements of paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(2) the survivor is entitled to a widowed parent's allowance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 39A(1A) the section applies to the death of the woman's husband`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply in cases where a woman's husband has died before 9 April 2001."
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 39A(1) the section applies`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            `s 37 both` `sch 3 pt I para 5 the contribution conditions for a widowed parent's allowance are satisfied` `s 39A(2) the survivor satisfies the requirements of paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`
            -- JUST FALSE when a condition fails: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance ... if the deceased ... satisfied the contribution conditions ... and—"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 39A applies only "where" subsection (1) holds

-- (3A) to (3D) Only one person is entitled in respect of one death. Where more than one would be, entitlement
-- is decided by (3C) and (3D). A candidate is a person who would, apart from (3A), be entitled.
-- src:1133 | (3A) Only one person is entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance in respect of one death.
-- src:1134 | (3B) Where, apart from subsection (3A), more than one person would be so entitled, entitlement is to be determined in accordance with subsections (3C) and (3D).
@ref s 39A(3B) (src:1133-1134)
DECLARE `s 39A Candidate` HAS
    `s 39A(3B) the kind of survivor` IS A `s 39A Kind of survivor`
    `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 39A(3D) is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 39A(3D)(c) the number of days as a member of the same household as the deceased` IS A NUMBER

-- (3D)(a) one of those persons who is a member of the same household is the deceased's spouse or civil
-- partner and is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in (2).
-- src:1136 | (3D) Where there is more than one person who is a member of the same household as the deceased and would (apart from subsection (3A)) be entitled—
-- src:1137 | (a) if one of those persons is the deceased’s spouse or civil partner and is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2), that person is entitled;
@ref s 39A(3D) (src:1136-1137)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
`s 39A(3D)(a) the household members who are the deceased's spouse or civil partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased` AND c's `s 39A(3D) is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2)` AND (c's `s 39A(3B) the kind of survivor` EQUALS `s 39A the surviving spouse` OR c's `s 39A(3B) the kind of survivor` EQUALS `s 39A the surviving civil partner`)) candidates

-- (3D)(b) the deceased's cohabiting partner who is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in (2).
-- src:1138 | (b) if there is no spouse or civil partner entitled under paragraph (a), the deceased’s cohabiting partner who is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2) is entitled (but this is subject to paragraphs (c) and (d));
@ref s 39A(3D) (src:1138)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
`s 39A(3D)(b) the household members who are the deceased's cohabiting partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased` AND c's `s 39A(3D) is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2)` AND c's `s 39A(3B) the kind of survivor` EQUALS `s 39A the surviving cohabiting partner`) candidates

-- (3D)(c) if more than one cohabiting partner is within (b), the one who has been a member of the same
-- household as the deceased for longest.
-- src:1139 | (c) if there is more than one cohabiting partner within paragraph (b), the cohabiting partner who has been a member of the same household as the deceased for longest is entitled;
@ref s 39A(3D) (src:1139)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
`s 39A(3D)(c) the cohabiting partners who have been members of the household for longest` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3D)(c) the number of days as a member of the same household as the deceased` EQUALS maximum (map (GIVEN d YIELD d's `s 39A(3D)(c) the number of days as a member of the same household as the deceased`) (`s 39A(3D)(b) the household members who are the deceased's cohabiting partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates))) (`s 39A(3D)(b) the household members who are the deceased's cohabiting partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates)

-- (3B) to (3D) The persons entitled, when more than one candidate would be entitled apart from (3A). JUST list:
-- the one person decided by (3C), (3D)(a), (3D)(b) or (3D)(c). NOTHING: the text does not decide (no household
-- member; two spouses or civil partners; no one within (a) or (b); or a tie that (3D)(d) leaves to the
-- Secretary of State). Fork F17 in NOTES.md.
-- src:1134 | (3B) Where, apart from subsection (3A), more than one person would be so entitled, entitlement is to be determined in accordance with subsections (3C) and (3D).
-- src:1135 | (3C) Where only one of those persons is a member of the same household as the deceased, that person is entitled.
-- src:1136 | (3D) Where there is more than one person who is a member of the same household as the deceased and would (apart from subsection (3A)) be entitled—
-- src:1137 | (a) if one of those persons is the deceased’s spouse or civil partner and is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2), that person is entitled;
-- src:1138 | (b) if there is no spouse or civil partner entitled under paragraph (a), the deceased’s cohabiting partner who is pregnant or entitled to child benefit as described in subsection (2) is entitled (but this is subject to paragraphs (c) and (d));
-- src:1139 | (c) if there is more than one cohabiting partner within paragraph (b), the cohabiting partner who has been a member of the same household as the deceased for longest is entitled;
-- src:1140 | (d) if there is more than one cohabiting partner within paragraph (b) and each partner has been a member of the same household as the deceased for the same length of time, the Secretary of State must determine who is entitled.
@ref s 39A(3B) (src:1134-1140)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`)
`s 39A(3B) the persons entitled` MEANS
    IF count candidates AT MOST 1
    THEN JUST candidates
    ELSE IF count (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased`) candidates) EQUALS 1
         THEN JUST (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased`) candidates)     -- (3C)
         ELSE IF count (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased`) candidates) AT LEAST 2
              THEN (IF count (`s 39A(3D)(a) the household members who are the deceased's spouse or civil partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates) EQUALS 1
                    THEN JUST (`s 39A(3D)(a) the household members who are the deceased's spouse or civil partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates)     -- (3D)(a)
                    ELSE IF count (`s 39A(3D)(a) the household members who are the deceased's spouse or civil partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates) AT LEAST 2
                         THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two or more spouses or civil partners within (a)
                         ELSE IF count (`s 39A(3D)(b) the household members who are the deceased's cohabiting partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates) EQUALS 1
                              THEN JUST (`s 39A(3D)(b) the household members who are the deceased's cohabiting partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates)     -- (3D)(b)
                              ELSE IF count (`s 39A(3D)(b) the household members who are the deceased's cohabiting partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates) AT LEAST 2
                                   THEN (IF count (`s 39A(3D)(c) the cohabiting partners who have been members of the household for longest` candidates) EQUALS 1
                                         THEN JUST (`s 39A(3D)(c) the cohabiting partners who have been members of the household for longest` candidates)     -- (3D)(c)
                                         ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): (3D)(d) leaves a tie to the Secretary of State to determine
                                   ELSE NOTHING)     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner within (a) or (b)
              ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no candidate is a member of the same household as the deceased

-- src:1133 | (3A) Only one person is entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance in respect of one death.
@ref s 39A(3A) (src:1133)
GIVEN candidate IS A `s 39A Candidate`
      candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(3A) the candidate is the one person entitled to a widowed parent's allowance in respect of the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 39A(3B) the persons entitled` candidates
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): see the rule above
    WHEN JUST entitled THEN
        IF elem candidate entitled
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Only one person is entitled to a widowed parent’s allowance in respect of one death."

-- (3D)(d) If there is more than one cohabiting partner within (b) and each has been a member of the same
-- household for the same length of time, the Secretary of State must determine who is entitled. (8) The
-- Secretary of State must issue a statement of the Secretary of State's policy with respect to making
-- determinations under (3D)(d). (6) The Secretary of State may by regulations prescribe: machinery.
-- src:1140 | (d) if there is more than one cohabiting partner within paragraph (b) and each partner has been a member of the same household as the deceased for the same length of time, the Secretary of State must determine who is entitled.
@ref s 39A(3D) (src:1140)
DECLARE `s 39A Party` IS ONE OF
    `s 39A(3D)(d) the Secretary of State`

DECLARE `s 39A Act` IS ONE OF
    `s 39A(3D)(d) determine who is entitled to the widowed parent's allowance`
    `s 39A(8) issue a statement of the Secretary of State's policy with respect to making determinations under subsection (3D)(d)`

@ref s 39A(3D) (src:1140)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39A(3D)(d) the Secretary of State has to determine who is entitled` MEANS
    (count (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `s 39A(3C) is a member of the same household as the deceased`) candidates) AT LEAST 2)
    AND (count (`s 39A(3D)(a) the household members who are the deceased's spouse or civil partner and are pregnant or entitled to child benefit` candidates) EQUALS 0)
    AND (count (`s 39A(3D)(c) the cohabiting partners who have been members of the household for longest` candidates) AT LEAST 2)

-- src:1140 | (d) if there is more than one cohabiting partner within paragraph (b) and each partner has been a member of the same household as the deceased for the same length of time, the Secretary of State must determine who is entitled.
@ref s 39A(3D) (src:1140)
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `s 39A Candidate`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 39A Party` `s 39A Act`
`s 39A(3D)(d) the Secretary of State must determine who is entitled` MEANS
    IF `s 39A(3D)(d) the Secretary of State has to determine who is entitled` candidates
    THEN PARTY `s 39A(3D)(d) the Secretary of State` MUST `s 39A(3D)(d) determine who is entitled to the widowed parent's allowance`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1158 | (8) The Secretary of State must issue a statement of the Secretary of State’s policy with respect to making determinations under subsection (3D)(d).
@ref s 39A(8) (src:1158)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 39A Party` `s 39A Act`
`s 39A(8) the Secretary of State must issue a statement of policy` MEANS
    PARTY `s 39A(3D)(d) the Secretary of State` MUST `s 39A(8) issue a statement of the Secretary of State's policy with respect to making determinations under subsection (3D)(d)`

@ref s 39A(8) (src:1158)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(8) the Secretary of State is required to issue a statement of policy` MEANS
    JUST TRUE     -- the text imposes this duty without condition

-- (4), (4A), (4B) The surviving spouse (civil partner, cohabiting partner) shall not be entitled to the
-- allowance for any period after she or he remarries or forms a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership,
-- or marries, but, subject to that, shall continue to be entitled for any period throughout which she or he
-- satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) or (b) [(a), (b) or (c) for a cohabiting partner] and is
-- under pensionable age. For a surviving civil partner the text names (2)(a) or (b) only, so (c) alone does
-- not continue the entitlement of a civil partner (finding 16 in NOTES.md).
-- src:1141 | (4) The surviving spouse shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he remarries or forms a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership, but, subject to that, the surviving spouse shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he—
-- src:1142 | (a) satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) or (b) above; and
-- src:1143 | (b) is under pensionable age.
-- src:1144 | (4A) The surviving civil partner shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he forms a subsequent civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership or marries, but, subject to that, the surviving civil partner shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he—
-- src:1145 | (a) satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) or (b) above; and
-- src:1146 | (b) is under pensionable age.
-- src:1147 | (4B) The surviving cohabiting partner shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he forms a subsequent cohabiting partnership or a civil partnership or marries, but, subject to that, the surviving cohabiting partner shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he—
-- src:1148 | (a) satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a), (b) or (c) above; and
-- src:1149 | (b) is under pensionable age.
@ref s 39A(4) (src:1141-1149)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 39A Kind of survivor`
      `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(b) on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(c) on the day` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(4) the survivor satisfies the requirements named for the kind of survivor` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 39A the surviving spouse` THEN `s 37 either` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) on the day` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(b) on the day`
    WHEN `s 39A the surviving civil partner` THEN `s 37 either` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) on the day` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(b) on the day`
    WHEN `s 39A the surviving cohabiting partner` THEN `s 37 either` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) on the day` (`s 37 either` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(b) on the day` `the survivor satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(c) on the day`)

-- src:1141 | (4) The surviving spouse shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he remarries or forms a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership, but, subject to that, the surviving spouse shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he—
-- src:1142 | (a) satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) or (b) above; and
-- src:1143 | (b) is under pensionable age.
-- src:1144 | (4A) The surviving civil partner shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he forms a subsequent civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership or marries, but, subject to that, the surviving civil partner shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he—
-- src:1145 | (a) satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a) or (b) above; and
-- src:1146 | (b) is under pensionable age.
-- src:1147 | (4B) The surviving cohabiting partner shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he forms a subsequent cohabiting partnership or a civil partnership or marries, but, subject to that, the surviving cohabiting partner shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he—
-- src:1148 | (a) satisfies the requirements of subsection (2)(a), (b) or (c) above; and
-- src:1149 | (b) is under pensionable age.
@ref s 39A(4) (src:1141-1149)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the survivor` IS A Person
      `the day on which the survivor remarries, forms a civil partnership, forms a cohabiting partnership, or marries` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `s 39A(4) the survivor satisfies the requirements named for the kind of survivor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(4) the survivor is entitled to the allowance on the day` MEANS
    IF (CONSIDER `the day on which the survivor remarries, forms a civil partnership, forms a cohabiting partnership, or marries`
        WHEN JUST later THEN `the day` ABOVE later
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be entitled to the allowance for any period after she or he remarries or forms a civil partnership or a cohabiting partnership"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 37 both` `s 39A(4) the survivor satisfies the requirements named for the kind of survivor` (JUST (`the day` BELOW (`the survivor`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)))
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall continue to be entitled to it for any period throughout which she or he— (a) satisfies the requirements ...; and (b) is under pensionable age"

-- (5) A widowed parent's allowance shall not be payable (a) for any period before the day on which the
-- survivor's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration
-- Act; or (b) for any period during which the survivor and a person whom she or he is not married to, or in a
-- civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
-- src:1150 | (5) A widowed parent’s allowance shall not be payable—
-- src:1151 | (a) for any period falling before the day on which the surviving spouse’s, civil partner’s or cohabiting partner’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act; ... or
-- src:1152 | (b) for any period during which the surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner and a person whom she or he is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners.
@ref s 39A(5) (src:1150-1152)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the survivor's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the survivor and a person whom she or he is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(5) the allowance is payable for the day` MEANS
    IF `the survivor and a person whom she or he is not married to, or in a civil partnership with, are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners on the day`
    THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A widowed parent’s allowance shall not be payable— ... (b) for any period during which the surviving spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner and a person whom she or he is not married to ... are living together as if they were a married couple or civil partners."
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day on which the survivor's entitlement is to be regarded as commencing by virtue of section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act`
         WHEN JUST commencing THEN
             IF `the day` BELOW commencing
             THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A widowed parent’s allowance shall not be payable— (a) for any period falling before the day on which the surviving spouse’s, civil partner’s or cohabiting partner’s entitlement is to be regarded as commencing"
             ELSE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only when the allowance is not payable
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the commencing day is for section 5(1)(k) of the Administration Act

-- (7) For the purposes of s 39A and s 39C, two persons are cohabiting partners if they are not married to, or
-- civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were married or in a civil partnership.
-- src:1157 | (7) For the purposes of this section and section 39C, two persons are cohabiting partners if they are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were married or in a civil partnership (and “cohabiting partnership” is to be read accordingly).
@ref s 39A(7) (src:1157)
GIVEN `the two persons are married to each other or are civil partners of each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the two persons are living together as if they were married or in a civil partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39A(7) the two persons are cohabiting partners` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the two persons are married to each other or are civil partners of each other`) AND `the two persons are living together as if they were married or in a civil partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "two persons are cohabiting partners if they are not married to, or civil partners of, each other but are living together as if they were married or in a civil partnership"

§§ `s 39C Rate of widowed parent's allowance`

-- (1) The weekly rate of a widowed parent's allowance is determined in accordance with ss 44 to 45AA and
-- Schedules 4A and 4B as they apply to a Category A retirement pension, subject to s 39C and s 46.
-- Seam S15: ssc3 s 46(2) asks whether the additional pension falls to be calculated under s 45 "by virtue of
-- section 39C(1)". It does for a widowed parent's allowance.
-- src:1162 | (1) The weekly rate of a widowed parent’s allowance shall be determined in accordance with the provisions of sections 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B below as they apply in the case of a Category A retirement pension, but subject, in particular, to the following provisions of this section and section 46 below.
@ref s 39C(1) (src:1162)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39C(1) the additional pension falls to be calculated under section 45 by virtue of this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `widowed parent's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 39C(1) speaks only of a widowed parent's allowance

-- (1A) In its application by virtue of (1), s 44(4) is read as if for the first amount specified in that
-- provision there were substituted a reference to the amount prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.
-- src:1163 | (1A) In its application by virtue of subsection (1) above, section 44(4) below is to be read as if for the first amount specified in that provision there were substituted a reference to the amount prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.
@ref s 39C(1A) (src:1163)
GIVEN `the amount prescribed for the purposes of subsection (1A) in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 39C(1A) the amount read in place of the first amount specified in section 44(4) in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount prescribed for the purposes of subsection (1A) in pounds`     -- NOTHING when not supplied: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the amount prescribed"

-- (3) In the application of ss 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B by virtue of (1): (a) where the deceased was
-- over pensionable age at death, references to the pensioner are references to the deceased; (b) where the
-- deceased was under pensionable age at death, references to the pensioner and the tax year in which he
-- attained pensionable age are references to the deceased and the tax year in which he or she died.
-- src:1165 | (3) In the application of sections 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B below by virtue of subsection (1) above —
-- src:1166 | (a) where the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner was over pensionable age at his or her death, references in those provisions to the pensioner shall be taken as references to the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner, and
-- src:1167 | (b) where the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner was under pensionable age at his or her death, references in those provisions to the pensioner and the tax year in which he attained pensionable age shall be taken as references to the deceased spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner and the tax year in which he or she died.
@ref s 39C(3) (src:1165-1167)
GIVEN `the deceased` IS A Person
      `the day on which the deceased died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 39C(3) the deceased was over pensionable age at death` MEANS
    `the day on which the deceased died` AT LEAST (`the deceased`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)

@ref s 39C(3) (src:1166-1167)
GIVEN `the deceased` IS A Person
      `the day on which the deceased died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 39C(3) the tax year read as the tax year in which the pensioner attained pensionable age` MEANS
    IF `s 39C(3) the deceased was over pensionable age at death` `the deceased` `the day on which the deceased died`
    THEN `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `s 23A(8) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the date begins` (`the deceased`'s `date of attaining pensionable age`)
    ELSE `Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `s 23A(8) the calendar year in which the tax year containing the date begins` `the day on which the deceased died`

-- (4) Where a widowed parent's allowance is payable to a person whose spouse, civil partner or cohabiting
-- partner dies after 5th October 2002, the additional pension falling to be calculated under ss 44 to 45AA and
-- Schedules 4A and 4B by virtue of (1) is one half of the amount which it would be apart from this subsection.
-- src:1168 | (4) Where a widowed parent’s allowance is payable to a person whose spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner dies after 5th October 2002, the additional pension falling to be calculated under sections 44 to 45AA and Schedules 4A and 4B below by virtue of subsection (1) above shall be one half of the amount which it would be apart from this subsection.
@ref s 39C(4) (src:1168)
GIVEN `the additional pension apart from subsection (4) in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day on which the spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 39C(4) the additional pension falling to be calculated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the additional pension apart from subsection (4) in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the additional pension is worked out under sections 44 to 45AA
    WHEN JUST amount THEN
        IF `the day on which the spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner died` ABOVE (Date 5 10 2002)
        THEN JUST (50% TIMES amount)
        ELSE JUST amount     -- subsection (4) does not apply to a death on or before 5 October 2002: the amount stands
